DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       This program is part of NNeettppbbmm(1).

       ppaammvvaalliiddaattee  copies a Netpbm image from Standard Input to Standard Out‐
       put, except that if there are certain violations of the image format in
       the input, ppaammvvaalliiddaattee fails _w_i_t_h_o_u_t _p_r_o_d_u_c_i_n_g _a_n_y _o_u_t_p_u_t.

       This  is  most  useful  in a pipeline, before a stage you don't want to
       start working on Netpbm input until it knows it can  get  all  the  way
       through  it.   For example, assume you are converting PPM images to PNG
       and you don't want to produce a partial  PNG  file  under  any  circum‐
       stance.  If you just use ppnnmmttooppnngg, and the PPM input is truncated half‐
       way through the raster, ppnnmmttooppnngg fails, but also produces about half of
       a  PNG  file.  To prevent that, pass your PPM input through ppaammvvaalliiddaattee
       on its way to ppnnmmttooppnngg.  Then, ppaammvvaalliiddaattee will fail, and  consequently
       the  pipeline  will fail, before ppnnmmttooppnngg has seen any input and there‐
       fore before ppnnmmttooppnngg has produced any output.

       These are the kinds of format violations ppaammvvaalliiddaattee detects:



       •      A purported sample value exceeds the declared maxval.

       •      The stream ends prematurely.


       This program works on multi-image streams,  producing  a  corresponding
       output stream.

       See ppaammffiixx for a way to salvage an invalid Netpbm image stream.



